onto a completely new environment without modifying it a little, or a lot. Oftentimes the dupletecture is larger, or smaller than real thing, or different elements, or features might be loaded bigger than others, sometimes dupletecture gets so twisted and warped until it's a freakish caricature of the original. One of the interesting twists on this architectural movement has been the creation of mega-high rises that are built in a baroque or a neoclassical style. Picture Versailles stretched 20 floors into the air, and you'll have some idea of what's going on.
直接放置在一个全新的环境中而不进行一点或大量的修改。通常，复制建筑比实物更大或更小，或者不同的元素或特征可能比其他部分更突出，有时复制建筑会被扭曲和变形，直到成为原型的怪异讽刺画。这种建筑运动中一个有趣的转折是创造了巴洛克或新古典主义风格的超高层建筑。想象一下凡尔赛宫被拉高了20层，你就会对正在发生的事情有所了解。

